From the Philippines to the wide world or Strawbag trip to the hearts of fashion fans
Straw-braided bags are a summer classic, which in recent years has become a hit product of its own, which has to hang on the hands of one of the right summer lovers, and to which merchants, regardless of its modest origin, have managed to weld an additional price tag suitable for the hit.
A bag braided from straw is probably one of those things that everyone has had once in their life and the possession of which has not caused special emotions.
It just exists, and if it doesn't, there's nothing broken.
Now, however, straw bags are making a real triumph, and fashion fans have exchanged their exquisite designer bags for the summer months with simple straw-braided bags.
At the same time, it is not only a beach bag, but today it is just as popular as a street bag, and braver women even walk to the office with it.
At this point, however, it is worth making it clear beforehand whether such a summer look is still sitting for the boss, or whether it is still worth pushing the notebook and the laptop into a slightly more formal sumadan.
Variegation, however, has made women's true summer love from straw bags.
For example, when reading foreign fashion blogs, the first thing that catches the eye is that fashion gourmets rush to the local market as the first thing on a holiday trip to the local market and buy themselves a straw bag, to which they are faithful throughout the holiday season, and which goes with them on the beach, in the market, and also when hanging out with girlfriends in the city.
Some bloggers are so generous that they buy a bigger pile of bags from the market and sell or give them away to their loyal readers.
At the same time, it is worth noting that there is so much demand for bags among readers that in the real world, women (and men!) would probably go after each other by hand in order to become a happy owner of some bags.
In some ways, such madness is also understandable, because it is rare when it is possible to buy yourself something that has risen to the status of a hit for only a few dozens of euros.
It is true that cunning merchants have also discovered an easy way to earn money here, and so finer luxury brands also sell straw bags for a few hundred and a thousand euros.
It's probably because richer customers don't have to feel like mere mortals promenading around with some cheap bags.
For example, it is possible to buy a straw bag that costs more than a thousand euros for Dolce & Gabbana.
Chanel's straw bag's interpretation, however, can be spent around 6000 euros.
However, unlike most fashion hits, straw bags do not come from some big fashion mecca, but their story started much further afield.
Indeed, straw bags are said to have originated in the distant Philippines, from where they have been carried around.
Braiding a bag of straw is first and foremost an export business there, and you don't see the locals walking around with them very often.
It is saidably dates from the 14th century and is quite similar to ordinary basket weaving.
However, since you don't have to weave a straw bag as strongly as a basket, you can weave patterns and other materials into them, which make the bag more personalized and thus more attractive.
For example, there have been especially trendy bags with colored ribbons or leather bands braided.
A letter of appreciation can first and foremost be sent by the actress Jane Birkin, of whom the biggest braided straw bag fan had never been seen before.
Namely, he matched a straw bag with all sorts of sets of clothes and didn't even think it's too much to go to the Cannes Film Festival.
However, with the popularity of bags today, it does not play a smaller role, but that taking care of them is a rooster head, and unlike all kinds of other sumadans, they do not have to be taken care of with special means, but water and a wet towel also do the trick.
As always in the case of trends, in addition to the classic appearance, brands have come up with all sorts of interpretations.
For example, if you wish, you can buy braided ridges made of straw or a tiny shoulder bag.
At the same time, it is worth remembering that a classic straw bag will never go out of fashion, but it does.
But what is a classic straw bag?
For centuries, it has been considered classic to have such a straw-braided bag that resembles a basket in its style, is open from the top, and there are short, as well as strain, handles.
Five healthy ice creams that are easy to make at home
Lifehack.org highlighted ways to prepare different types of ice creams at home that contain fewer calories than store ice creams.
Lemon and buttermilk ice cream - in a large bowl, whisk the lemon juice with the sugar, add the buttermilk and whipped cream and mix everything into an even mass, place the mixture in the refrigerator.
Chocolate and peanut ice cream - blend Greek yogurt, frozen bananas, cocoa powder and maple syrup into an even mass.
Then add a little peanut butter to the mixture and blend the mixture for a few seconds.
Ice cream is ready to eat immediately.
Peach ice cream - in a bowl, mix the fat-free milk, sugar substitute, egg, frozen or ordinary peach slices and almond extract into an even mass and place the resulting mixture in the refrigerator to harden.
Coconut ice cream - blend coconut milk, coconut flakes, vanilla extract, maple syrup and frozen bananas and place the resulting mixture in the refrigerator.
Banana ice cream - in a bowl, mix frozen banana pieces with low-fat milk into an even mass, serve with walnuts and consume immediately.
